{"ts": 0.317437, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 1 · Where am I?\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m1.4\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 269}
{"ts": 0.319964, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m1.4 — what just happened\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nWhen you type \u001b[92mwhoami\u001b[0m and press Enter:\r\n\r\n  1. The terminal hands your line to \u001b[36mthe shell\u001b[0m.\r\n  2. The shell looks for a program named \u001b[92mwhoami\u001b[0m.\r\n  3. It runs it.\r\n  4. The program prints to \u001b[36mstandard output\u001b[0m — your screen.\r\n  5. The shell shows the prompt again, ready for the next command.\r\n\r\nThe shell is not \"Unix.\" It is a program — a \u001b[36mcommand interpreter\u001b[0m.\r\nThe terminal is a window that lets you talk to the shell. The program\r\n\u001b[92mwhoami\u001b[0m is a third thing — it runs, prints, and exits.\r\n\r\nYou will keep these three apart for the rest of this tutor:\r\n  \u001b[36mterminal\u001b[0m  →  \u001b[36mshell\u001b[0m  →  \u001b[36mprogram\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to take Stage 1's gate.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 769}
{"ts": 0.320449, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
{"ts": 0.341349, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[95mnext\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ go on\u001b[0m   \u001b[95mshow\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ this screen again\u001b[0m   \u001b[95mprev\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ back\u001b[0m   \u001b[95mquit\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ save and leave\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
